This macro enables console logging and provides AI agent I/O capabilities with GUI configuration.
DESIGNED FOR CONTINUOUS OPERATION - keeps FreeCAD GUI open with AI monitoring active.

FREECAD PYTHON DOCUMENTATION & RESOURCES FOR AI AGENTS:
============================================================

OFFICIAL DOCUMENTATION:
- FreeCAD Python API: https://freecad.github.io/SourceDoc/
- Python Scripting Tutorial: https://wiki.freecad.org/Python_scripting_tutorial
- Power Users Hub: https://wiki.freecad.org/Power_users_hub
- FreeCAD API Reference: https://wiki.freecad.org/FreeCAD_API

ESSENTIAL MODULES:
- App (FreeCAD): Document, objects, geometry operations
- Gui (FreeCADGui): View operations, selection, GUI interaction
- Part: CAD modeling, shapes, boolean operations
- Draft: 2D drafting tools
- Sketcher: Constraint-based sketching

COMMON PATTERNS:
- Create document: App.newDocument('Name')
- Add object: App.ActiveDocument.addObject('Type', 'Name')
- Access selection: Gui.Selection.getSelection()
- Recompute: App.ActiveDocument.recompute()

BEST PRACTICES:
1. Always check App.ActiveDocument exists before operations
2. Use try/except for error handling
3. Call recompute() after geometry changes
4. Access objects by Name, not Label (Label can have duplicates)
5. Check object.isDerivedFrom('Type') before type-specific operations

LEARNING RESOURCES:
- FreeCAD Forum: https://forum.freecad.org/
- Python Console (built-in): View -> Panels -> Python console
- Macro Recorder: Macro -> Macro recording -> Record actions
- Example Macros: https://wiki.freecad.org/Macros_recipes

3D MODEL LIBRARY RESOURCES (AI REFERENCE):
============================================================
The AI Bridge provides context about indexed 3D model libraries at startup.

RESOURCE FILES (Machine-Readable):
- 3D_Library_Resources.json: Complete reference for 3D library system
  * Database location and schema
  * External sources (FreeCAD Library, GrabCAD, Thingiverse, McMaster-Carr)
  * Supported formats (FCStd, STEP, STL, BREP)
  * Search capabilities and AI usage patterns
  * Access macros: 047_3D_Library_Indexer, 048_3D_Library_Browser

DATABASE LOCATION:
- Windows: %APPDATA%\\FreeCAD\\3d_library_index.db
- Linux/Mac: ~/.FreeCAD/3d_library_index.db

AI USAGE PATTERN:
1. Check if database exists on startup
2. Reference 3D_Library_Resources.json for capabilities
3. When user needs parts: Suggest 048_3D_Library_Browser
4. When user needs to index: Suggest 047_3D_Library_Indexer
5. Can query database directly using Python sqlite3 if needed

NOTE: These are REFERENCE resources. AI should not create/modify library
      macros or database unless explicitly requested by the user.
"""

__Name__ = 'AI Bridge - Self-Learning & Self-Healing'
__Comment__ = 'The AI Bridge: lets an external AI agent drive this FreeCAD session over a JSONL command channel, with a live activity view, learning store and local Ollama support'
